Gilgameš lay down, night's rest upon him:
My friend, I have seen a second —
33b	beyond the first dream I saw, this one is full of dread.
34	Adad kept crying out; the earth was rumbling;
35	the day was hooded dark; darkness came out;
36	lightning flashed; fire broke out;
37	the flames billowed thick; it was raining death.
38	At the crying of Adad I was going faint;
39	the daylight dimmed, and I did not know which way I walked.
40	Then somehow the blaze burned down; the fire went out;
41	the flames kept falling, turned to cinders;
42	the darkness brightened; the god came o[u]t.

My heart does n[ot] carry me off i[n] my own prowess(?);
79	Šamaš(?) has told me: 'Go — I am w[it]h you(?).'
80	Do not fear, Enkidu; watch over me;
81	a bat[t]le you have never known — let me make my heart perform it(?)!
